# Room overlap

Organizers may put two sessions in one space at overlapping times. That state is supported, not advised.

`accept_session` and `assign_session` must not refuse the write. Keep the locks that serialise writes. A room overlap is `RoomBookingConflict` (`ConflictType.SPACE_OVERLAP`), shown in the existing booking-conflict UI (timetable conflict panel and problems page). It is not a `PlacementRejection` and not an application error.

Do not open a change that refuses an overlapping room booking. The participant schedule and the printed timetable show both sessions side by side in the room.
